    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d94">

                <pb facs="0096" n="90" sameAs="frus:frus1942v03/pg90"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">857.857/388</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Secretary of
                        State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-11-20">November 20, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Ambassador of Norway came in following his recent return from London. He
                    repeated the same views about their shipping situation, which he had expressed
                    to Assistant Secretary Long. I said that it had been agreed that certain tonnage
                    lost in the Allied cause would be replaced by ships from the United States and
                    that the only thing remaining was to work out the details of the agreement as to
                    the kind of ships and the number, et cetera. The purpose of the agreement was
                        <pb facs="0097" n="91" xml:id="pg91"/> twofold, namely, to replace tonnage
                    lost and to give employment to several hundred Norwegian seamen, engineers, et
                    cetera, who are in this country at the present time because their ships had been
                    sunk.</p>
                <p>I stated that every effort would be made to bring this matter to an early
                    conclusion.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ordell</hi>] H[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >ull</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
